<div class="page">
    <div style="display: flex; justify-content: space-between; align-items: flex-start; margin-bottom: 30px;">
        <div style="font-size: 24pt; font-weight: bold;">Production success</div>
    </div>
    <img src="placeholder_image_5.jpg" alt="Production line" style="width: 100%; height: auto; margin-bottom: 30px;">
    <p class="body-text" style="font-size: 16pt; font-weight: bold;">ABB provide power protection to Australasia's leading forest products company.</p>
    <div style="margin-top: 50px;">
        <div class="content-grid">
            <div class="column">
                <h3 style="font-size: 14pt; font-weight: bold;">ABB's AVC protects the industrial microwave generators during the production process.</h3>
                <p class="body-text">ABB's technology has provided Carter Holt Harvey's Laminated Veneer Lumber (LVL) Mill in Marsden Point (two hours drive north of New Zealand's largest city, Auckland) with the microwave generators from falling. This solution has provided greater productivity and decreased magnetron replacement.</p>
                <p class="body-text">VL is a step-by-step process and if one production line fails, the whole process can be derailed. This was evident for Carter Holt Harvey (CHH), and the need to install ABB's Active Voltage Conditioner (AVC) was necessary to prevent future voltage disturbances from occurring.</p>
                <p class="body-text">The CHH Wood Products NZ business group manufactures and markets a full range of wood based building products, including timber, plywood, laminated veneer lumber (LVL), particleboard, and a range of interior decorative products, supplied from nine major manufacturing stations spread throughout New Zealand.</p>
            </div>
            <div class="column">
                <p class="body-text">manufacture) so the glue cures faster. This allows the factory to make more ply-wood than if they waited for the natural cure time of the glue. Voltage fluctuations can cause the glue to fail, which is a trip to which has halting the production line, causing production loss and requiring costly replacement of parts.</p>
                <p class="body-text">CHH had specific requirements that were product reliability, increased yield, lower running costs, and increased machine uptime. To achieve this, they re-invested in a power protection system for the plant would be required.</p>
                <p class="body-text">Therefore, ABB's Active Voltage Conditioner (AVC) was installed to condition the incoming power to the microwave units.</p>
                <p class="body-text">With Northland's power (including the CHH plant) being supplied through Auckland, the instance moved the plant to a more reliable and more consistent power supply, and the AVC has provided greater reliability and productivity for the plant.</p>
                <p class="body-text">In the four months following the installation, only one magnetron has been replaced.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>

<div class="page">
