                <p>TMD analyzed all the data for last time and determined that the voltage sags in its main power equipment, for connection units, and for other existing factories in <span data-field="location_city">{{ location_city }}</span>, <span data-field="location_country">{{ location_country }}</span>. PCS100 UPS due to the proven market and cost performance in power quality and protection.</p>
                <p>The PCS100 AVC is a battery free solution leading to less maintenance costs, no battery replacement, which poses one of its advantages, along with sag and swell protection and continuous voltage protection. The PCS100 UPS is 1+1 topology, which demands only a small footprint, and its applications such as motors, drives, transformers and tools. It also provides pro-tection during deep sag and swell, plus outages between seconds and minutes depending on storage (super capacitors or batteries) and system loading.</p>
            </div>
        </div>
        <div style="width: 48%;">
            <div class="sub-heading">Customers comments</div>
            <div class="body-text">
                <p>Mr. Shinji Kubomae, TMD's Special Production Engineering Group, Pro-cess and Manufacturing Engineering Department, stated, "Since PCS100 AVC was introduced, we were able to be flexible in deciding whether or not to have full back up to the protected load. As a result, we achieved significant cost reduction, as well as saving energy and space for the new factory."</p>
                <p>In addition, TMD experienced other ben-efits from working with ABB, including a high level of reliability, a tight timescale for implementation, and a high level of support required to be in place prior to the be-ginning of winter, in order to test the full extremes of environmental forces.</p>
